//! The `opacity` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property sets the opacity
//! of an element. Opacity is the degree to which content behind an element is hidden, and is the
//! opposite of transparency.
//!
//! Initial: 1. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: map to the range [0,1].
//!
//! Grammar: <opacity-value>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-4/#propdef-opacity
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/opacity
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

